# R96E1 receipt — item 2: the rev guard refuses before any grading
#
# instrument: same frozen measure-v96.py (sha256 e0da9935...) as R96E1-honest.out.
# Every work directory below is either pre-created empty or absent; the counter's
# rev guard runs before the work-dir check, so a refusal cannot touch it.
#
# Part A: the three required refusals, --repo the real lane (read-only).
# Part B: the F2 attack (a clone with a staged, uncommitted inverted note):
#   --rev '' must not grade the index.
# Part C: why the 40-hex-unresolvable token differs: git rev-parse semantics at 2.56.0.

### command: python3 -I measure-v96-frozen.py --repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin --rev "" --work rev1
C1_SETUP rev-not-a-commit-id
C1_R96_PASS=false
EXIT=2
work dir rev1 entries after the refusal: 0

### command: python3 -I measure-v96-frozen.py --repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin --rev master --work rev2
C1_SETUP rev-not-a-commit-id
C1_R96_PASS=false
EXIT=2
work dir rev2 entries after the refusal: 0

### command: python3 -I measure-v96-frozen.py --repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin --rev deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef --work rev3
C1_SETUP spec-absent-at-rev
C1_R96_PASS=false
EXIT=2
work dir rev3 entries after the refusal: 0

$ git -C clone-staged status --porcelain
M  corpus/knowledge/mutation-case-fleet-sources-census.md
$ git -C clone-staged diff --cached --stat
 .../mutation-case-fleet-sources-census.md          | 24 +++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
$ python3 -I measure-v96-frozen.py --repo clone-staged --rev "" --work work-staged-empty
C1_SETUP rev-not-a-commit-id
C1_R96_PASS=false
EXIT=2
work dir entries: 0
$ python3 -I measure-v96-frozen.py --repo clone-staged --rev master --work work-staged-empty
C1_SETUP rev-not-a-commit-id
C1_R96_PASS=false
EXIT=2
work dir entries: 0

# Part C — git rev-parse semantics that make `rev-unresolvable` unreachable for a
# syntactically valid 40-hex name (git 2.56.0, /usr/bin/git):
$ git -C clone-honest rev-parse deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
EXIT=0
$ git -C clone-honest rev-parse --verify deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
EXIT=0
$ git -C clone-honest cat-file -e deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef
EXIT=1
$ git -C clone-honest rev-parse --verify 'deadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef^{object}'
fatal: Needed a single revision
EXIT=128

# A 40-hex name that is not an object is echoed by `rev-parse` with exit 0, so the
# counter's `_resolved = git(repo, "rev-parse", rev); if rc != 0: die("rev-unresolvable")`
# does not fire: the run continues to the first blob read and dies later with
# `spec-absent-at-rev` (still exit 2, still C1_R96_PASS=false, nothing graded,
# work dir untouched). `rev-unresolvable` remains reachable only when git itself
# fails (e.g. --repo is not a repository).
